./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:3:description: Define a currency in your workspace's settings
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:7:As a workspace admin, you can choose a default currency for your employees' expense reports, and we’ll automatically convert any expenses into that currency.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:10:- Currency settings for a workspace apply to all expenses under that workspace. If you need different default currencies for certain employees, creating separate workspaces and configuring the currency settings is best.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:11:- As an admin, the currency settings you establish in the workspace will take precedence over any currency settings individual users may have in their accounts.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:12:- Currency is a workspace-level setting, meaning the currency you set will determine the currency for all expenses submitted on that workspace.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:14:# Select the currency on a workspace
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:28:Please note the currency setting on an individual workspace is overridden when you submit a report on a group workspace.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:32:Using data from Open Exchange Rates, Expensify converts expenses from one currency to another using the average rate on the day the expense occurred. The conversion rate can vary depending on when the expense occurred since it is determined after the market closes on that specific date.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:42:Then, set the default currency for that workspace to match the currency in which the employees are reimbursed.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:44:For example, if you have employees in the US, France, Japan, and India, you’d want to create four separate workspaces, add the employees to each, and then set the corresponding currency for each workspace.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:50:If you're traveling to foreign countries during a reporting period and making purchases in various currencies, each expense is imported with the currency of the purchase.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:52:On your expense report, Expensify will automatically convert each expense to the default currency set for the group workspace.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:54:## How does the currency of an expense impact the conversion rate?
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:56:Expenses entered in a foreign currency are automatically converted to the default currency on your workspace. The conversion uses the day’s average trading rate pulled from [Open Exchange Rates](https://openexchangerates.org/).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Currency.md:58:If you want to bypass the exchange rate conversion, you can manually enter an expense in your default currency instead.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Set-Up-Invoicing.md:22:To set the currency, head to _**Settings** > **Workspaces** > **Reports**_. This will add default report-level fields to your invoices.  You can see these at the bottom of the [**Reports**](https://expensify.com/reports) page.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspaces/Create-a-group-workspace.md:7:A workspace is the set of rules, settings, and spending limits for expense reports in your organization. This includes the unique expense categories and tags, budgets, currency and tax settings, etc. that all workspace members will use. A workspace also defines the approval workflow for your employees, as well as the accounting connection if using an accounting software integration.

